 p('<b>Actual finite quotients.</b> For every finite target group H and h in H, Lean embeds an actual extension of K of degree order(h) into the actual algebraic closure. Continuous restriction to that finite intermediate field sends Frobenius to its actual cyclic Galois-group generator. Cyclic-group equivalences map the generator to h. Density gives uniqueness. Thus evaluation is a bijection on continuous homomorphisms into every finite H, including non-Abelian H. [pcc:unverified]'),
 p('<b>Actual continuous cocycles.</b> The action is an actual continuous homomorphism rho:Gamma→Aut(M), with M and Aut(M) discrete. All continuous functions satisfying c(st)=c(s) rho(s)(c(t)) form the actual cocycle group. Each cocycle has an actual continuous graph homomorphism into M semidirect Aut(M). The finite-target theorem constructs a graph homomorphism with any prescribed Frobenius value; its automorphism projection equals rho by density. Its first component supplies the cocycle. Graph uniqueness proves injectivity. No cocycle, H1 value, rank or duality conclusion is assumed. [pcc:unverified]'),
